<title>USA: U.S. say Japan auto agreement opening markets.</title>
<headline>U.S. say Japan auto agreement opening markets.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. trade officials said on Thursday that the 1995 agreement with Japan on automotive trade has significantly opened markets, but more progress was needed on dealerships and on deregulation of the parts market.</p>
<p>&quot;By virtually any measure this agreement has been a success in significantly opening the Japanese auto and auto parts market,&quot; a U.S. trade official said after the two sides reviewed the agreement in talks in San Francisco.</p>
</text>
